            "**In the breastfed infant, treat the mother's nipples simultaneously or the infection ping-pongs: miconazole 2% or nystatin cream to both nipples and areolae after every feed for 14 days**, with **oral fluconazole for the mother (150-400 mg loading then 100 mg daily for 10-14 days)** for deep persistent breast pain. **How routinely to do this is disputed** - nipple candidiasis is over-diagnosed and most sore nipples are due to a poor latch, tongue-tie, vasospasm or bacterial infection - **so assess the latch and examine the nipple first, and treat the pair together when the infant genuinely has thrush.**",
